# 1. MISSION

LEAN-1 through LEAN-5 were designed to transform 5TOT Đà Nẵng into a simple, professional and business-correct Student award management platform.

The previous phases targeted:

- LEAN-1: Simplified Student declaration forms and automatic declaration numbering.
- LEAN-2: Direct inline human Pass/Fail review.
- LEAN-3: Contextual supplementation and reassessment.
- LEAN-4: School recommendation, intentional selection and one-time forwarding.
- LEAN-5: City shared review, Committee experience, status consistency and responsive UX.

LEAN-6 is the final integration and acceptance phase.

**The objective is to prove that these changes work together across real application lifecycle transitions, not merely that individual screens look correct.**

Verify the system as if conducting a complete Student 5-Good award selection season.

A real Student must be able to register, declare achievements and submit.

An authorized School reviewer must be able to review the actual submission, request supplementation, record recommendations and forward a consolidated official list.

An authorized City reviewer must be able to independently assess forwarded applications.

An authorized Committee member must be able to inspect accumulated results and record an official decision.

Collective applications must follow their separate approved route directly to City.

All operations must preserve:

- Actual database persistence.
- Correct user permissions.
- Correct institution scope.
- Accurate review results.
- Evidence integrity.
- Audit attribution.
- Authorized state transitions.
- Proper separation of official decisions.
- No cross-role information leakage.
- No Demo/Real contamination.

The system must remain LEAN.

Do not recreate previously removed redundant operations merely to make testing easier.

